+
+Device Allocation
+-----------------
+Application can specify which device (CPU, GPU, or any other devices detected by SYCL) to use in file "src/cpp/flann/algorithms/dpcpp/kdtree_dpcpp_3d_index.dp.cpp", by passing specific device id to the line "dpct::get_device()".
+Device id and name can be checked via "get_device_info()" as shown in below commented codes.
+
+```bash
+void KDTreeDpcpp3dIndex<Distance>::uploadTreeToGpu()
+{
+    if (!init) {
+        q_ct1 = dpct::get_device(0).default_queue();
+        policy = oneapi::dpl::execution::make_device_policy(q_ct1);
+        init = true;
+    }
+    //dpct::device_info dev_info;
+    //dpct::get_device(0).get_device_info(dev_info);
+    //printf("--=============Device info %s \n", dev_info.get_name());
+    //printf("max work group %d, %d hz, %d eu\n", dev_info.get_max_work_group_size(), dev_info.get_max_clock_frequency(), dev_info.get_max_compute_units());
+```
+
+Limitations
+-----------
+* So far DPCPP is enabled for 3-dimension only. Other dimensions are not supported.
+* An overhead of milliseconds introduced for the creation of kdtree dpc++ tree since the tree index is built over sorted points.
+  - For applications that create trees frequently, a faster sorting mechanism need to be implemented. One option is to adopt bitonic-sort, sample codes available here <https://github.com/oneapi-src/oneAPI-samples/blob/bed8a563ace4a31d00a4f1055f65d680fa4fe0a8/DirectProgramming/DPC%2B%2B/GraphTraversal/bitonic-sort/src/bitonic-sort.cpp>
+  - For applications that don’t create trees often, this overhead could be just ignored, with a great compensation from reduced latency in knn searching.
+
+Known Issues
+------------
+* Build tests fails with DPCPP disabled, "-DBUILD_DPCPP_LIB=OFF -DBUILD_TESTS=ON". The cause of this issue could be, when DPCPP is disabled, the software is built with GCC 10 and gtest headers failed to build with this compiler. See googletest issue [#3383](https://github.com/google/googletest/issues/3384)
